I will examine the current database adapter connections to check how they are locked and closed. Let's inspect `DatabaseConnectionPool.kt`:

```kotlin
class DatabaseConnectionPool(private val dbPath: String) {
    private val pool = ArrayDeque<Connection>()

    fun getConnection(): Connection {
        // Missing synchronization lock wrapper
        return pool.removeFirstOrNull() ?: DriverManager.getConnection(dbPath)
    }
}
```

The issue is that connections are retrieved from the pool without proper synchronization locks. Under heavy concurrent execution, multiple threads can access the same connection, causing read-write collision locks. We need to implement a synchronized check and wrap operations in a thread-safe connection allocator.

